# lyric-harness: three classes of JSON that must NOT be autoformatted, for the
# same reason src/app.js and scripts/_voice_parts_data.js are excluded above —
# their exact BYTES are gated elsewhere, so a reflow breaks the gate.
#
# corpus/**        provenance-gated. Every corpus file has a row in
#                  lyric-harness/data/sources.tsv recording its hash
#                  (corpus/fas_hafez.json: sha256 a87fc7ed), and
#                  quality/audit_corpus.py check C fails the build when a
#                  recorded hash drifts. Reformatting would change the hash of
#                  a file whose whole purpose is to be the thing the hash
#                  names.
# data/**          vendored and generated: NLTK tagger models we did not
#                  author, a build report, and a feature cache.
# matrix_eval.json generated eval output, rewritten by quality/eval_matrix.py.
#
# The BLUEPRINTS are deliberately NOT excluded. They are authored declarations,
# they are parsed rather than byte-compared, and they should be formatted like
# any other source we write.
lyric-harness/corpus
lyric-harness/data
lyric-harness/quality/matrix_eval.json
